{
  "id": null,
  "uid": "shipment-service-overview",
  "title": "shipment-service Overview",
  "description": "Shipment tracking service (extracted from OMS, Phase 4 of the microservices-prep plan): HTTP traffic, Kafka consumer lag, transactional outbox, JVM, and DB pool. Generated to match the metrics exposed at /actuator/prometheus - see application.properties and OutboxMetrics.java. Companion to oms-overview.json and product-service-overview.json, not a replacement - filtered by application=\"shipment-service\" throughout so it never mixes with other services' metrics on the same Prometheus instance. Unlike product-service's dashboard, this one includes a consumer-lag panel and splits HTTP metrics by role=\"web\" - shipment-service (unlike product-service) has a real web/worker split (OrderConfirmedShipmentConsumer runs only on worker pods; Tomcat still runs on worker pods too per docs/process-roles.md, which is exactly why the HTTP panels filter role=\"web\" explicitly rather than trusting an unfiltered query to only ever see web-pod traffic).",
  "tags": [
    "oms",
    "shipment-service"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Overview",
      "type": "row",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
